    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "The user wanted the current/latest Rails gem version information as shown on RubyGems (version, release date, required Ruby version, license) and the first five runtime dependencies (not development) with their version requirements in the exact on-page order. A reasonable user would be flexible about minor formatting, but not flexible about missing required metadata fields or providing unsupported/possibly incorrect values for them.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor phrasing/formatting (bullets vs table), and adding a parenthetical note like “from prior step” are cosmetic and don’t affect usability.\n\nCritical issues: The task explicitly requires reporting required Ruby version and license for the latest Rails version. In the provided DOM evidence, the agent only visited the dependencies page (https://rubygems.org/gems/rails/versions/8.1.3.1/dependencies). That DOM confirms the latest version label “8.1.3.1 (latest)” and the release date “July 29, 2026,” and it clearly shows the runtime dependencies table. However, this DOM state does NOT display “Required Ruby version” or “License.” The agent nonetheless reports “Required Ruby version: >= 3.2.0” and “License: MIT,” attributing license to a “prior step’s Gem info page,” but no such step/page exists in the action history or DOM models provided. Therefore those two metadata fields are unsupported and could be incorrect (i.e., effectively a fabrication relative to available evidence).\n\nWhat the agent did correctly: It successfully accessed RubyGems without signing in/downloading, identified the latest version (8.1.3.1) and its release date (July 29, 2026), and accurately listed the first five runtime dependencies in the displayed order with correct requirements: actioncable, actionmailbox, actionmailer, actionpack, actiontext, each with “= 8.1.3.1.” It also did not list more than five dependencies.\n\nOverall outcome: Because two of the four required metadata items (required Ruby version and license) are not verifiably obtained from the actual visited RubyGems page(s) and appear to be asserted without evidence, the agent did not fully deliver the requested latest-version metadata. Despite getting the dependencies correct, missing/unsupported required metadata is a core deliverable, so the task is not successfully completed from the user’s perspective.",
